            "section": "The_Girl_who-ayed_with_Fire_split_006.html",
            "paragraph": 126,
            "part": 1,
            "chapter": null,
            "page": "8",
            "text": "“He’s a fine man who beats his wife,” Salander said.\nElla gave Salander a sharp look and went to the other end of the bar to serve some local customers.\nSalander stayed for ten minutes with her nose in Dimensions . She had known that she had a photographic memory since before she reached puberty, and because of it she was very different from her classmates. She had never revealed this to anyone—except to Blomkvist in a moment of weakness. She already knew the text of Dimensions in Mathematics by heart and was dragging the book around mainly because it represented a physical link to Fermat, as if the book had become some kind of talisman.",
